# Binary files, marked so git never applies line-ending conversion to them.
#
# This is load-bearing for the fixtures rather than tidiness. A hand-built PDF
# records byte offsets in its xref table, so a checkout that turned every LF
# into CRLF would shift every object past the first newline and leave the file
# claiming an object is somewhere it is not. Git guesses "text" for these
# because they are largely ASCII, and on Windows that guess silently produces
# corrupt fixtures on clone.
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wasm binary
*.gz binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
